 "reading": "the blit-hash law: composite = the kernel's HUD composite; blit = sha256 of to_blit(composite) (BGR, top-down); to_blit is a bijection (from_blit(to_blit(c))==c), so a byte corrupted between the kernel and the blit moves the blit witness and breaks the round-trip — a picture reaching the screen without passing through the kernel is detectable",
